6518777} {:answer/id #uuid "56105024-507d-5779-8bfb-522422369448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2d/2d5356db4c62ed3cd1b0fd068f5d16b8ef6a3b8750011ca37ca3657ed2eaab28.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518786} {:answer/id #uuid "94538c99-4a36-5413-b710-fcab9dfdd249" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e3/e3540bee55bf4207205efc609a695d4222c7707e614c86bfa8cb50b22b524d5d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518809} {:answer/id #uuid "9cd868e0-9e5d-5768-8b1a-bb8fe5d92407" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ed/ed2c4c2be8527c466b58b3c56d15559161e05dccdbcaaaf380320347f367bc47.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04b689a3-39ce-59dd-8039-cf17d3a57d17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/98/987e9aabd76d28c679efb27b92a2536d103e99eb3f915e6731ec37c56286876f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518764} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c4be32b-ebec-539c-b41e-ace6fb5e23bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518800}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b5efd26b-a36e-5669-8d57-24827ceb919a" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=2 x y\\,i-2 x^{2}\\,j$ at the indicated points?" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(1,- \\frac{1}{2}),(-1,\\frac{3}{2}),$ and $(1,\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=2 x y\\,i-2 x^{2}\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1,- \\frac{1}{2}) & =\\left((2)(1)\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left((-2)(1)^{2}\\right)\\,j=-i-2\\,j \\\\ F(-1,\\frac{3}{2}) & =\\left((2)(-1)\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left((-2)(-1)^{2}\\right)\\,j=-3\\,i-2\\,j \\\\ F(1,\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\left((2)(1)\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left((-2)(1)^{2}\\right)\\,j=i-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](images/98/987e9aabd76d28c679efb27b92a2536d103e99eb3f915e6731ec37c56286876f.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ccd2293-eb0e-5503-8406-7eaa88cc133f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0c/0cc1d91f18ad1c335e4a9a95a7c97a0bb899597af82abb1ffdf7c0650200e9eb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699577} {:answer/id #uuid "223c5e59-3a53-518e-99d2-280a2f535ea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2c/2c1666e7a50748cd375ce556176ceb7a2edeb8c5d837cbfb593a6dae6cccab54.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699579} {:answer/id #uuid "63de9413-df4d-5a79-ba67-9ca222d41e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ab/ab38dc8884f5e665d31b40193057d5af1665d1b0d582aca85cad2ee5fee8ed3c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699584} {:answer/id #uuid "6dee476e-780e-50ab-b392-8f62f9c3df96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f4/f4cc453b7166e4b7cde1a3ad12c8aa6b25c7419e1447a533b4cf40105aa359e4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699585} {:answer/id #uuid "8a4f82b3-02f8-5c61-94fa-c05d38cda737" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1f/1f30a5bd1c3094e9f37b157de9ddc1aea376bf94f426fb7010b343213f80ab2c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63de9413-df4d-5a79-ba67-9ca222d41e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ab/ab38dc8884f5e665d31b40193057d5af1665d1b0d582aca85cad2ee5fee8ed3c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699584} :answer-field/id #uuid "73378799-4cc1-54e0-af58-da11ea9dc550" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699586}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02bb3cbb-abee-5c30-8079-ac2b1489215f" :question/problem "Which diagram represents\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=-x\\,\\mathbf i-y\\,\\mathbf j\n$$\n\nat $A=(-2,1)$, $B=(1,2)$, and $C=(2,-2)$?\n\nEvaluate the two components at each point, then place the tail of its vector at that point. All diagrams use the same scale, with one unit per grid interval." :question/worked-solution "Substitute each point into $\\mathbf F(x,y)=-x\\,\\mathbf i-y\\,\\mathbf j$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(-2,1)&=-(-2)\\,\\mathbf i-(1)\\,\\mathbf j=2\\,\\mathbf i-\\mathbf j \\\\\n\\mathbf F(1,2)&=-(1)\\,\\mathbf i-(2)\\,\\mathbf j=-\\mathbf i-2\\,\\mathbf j \\\\\n\\mathbf F(2,-2)&=-(2)\\,\\mathbf i-(-2)\\,\\mathbf j=-2\\,\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlace each tail at its point: from $A$ go 2 units right and 1 down; from $B$ go 1 left and 2 down; from $C$ go 2 left and 2 up. The vectors point toward the origin. The correct diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/ab/ab38dc8884f5e665d31b40193057d5af1665d1b0d582aca85cad2ee5fee8ed3c.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699580 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bb90f32-89f2-5d99-9737-5e9e1ca8c70c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/05/05f03f531dbac4d3cfec041e444c47ce2d2ec6b5a01b8d316fe089d37ba9afcc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699576} {:answer/id #uuid "8912ac65-e717-5381-9bf6-2d58552daf10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bb/bbb0d965c7ec72ee8008b34972172af8cc5635df3d963dd27183a8f21b7f416d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699588} {:answer/id #uuid "8b30d0ac-2872-508b-b8fe-3739c8550d9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/45/45d92334e0129a9b3d3262664074b630066573703fef55c6bc804ec717066e69.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699590} {:answer/id #uuid "9b3461fd-6a84-5a93-bcaf-0ee5845013f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/eb/eb9cc13997a1fb7b1c56018ceb3df13d1d87033f16b607b85fa48e113a52c802.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699594} {:answer/id #uuid "e2d82c8a-464c-5b59-ba7d-24915ff57000" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/40/4059b6c9b926eea8ec523769d4858715f28ae316627f111fe08ca721df17ed28.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8912ac65-e717-5381-9bf6-2d58552daf10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bb/bbb0d965c7ec72ee8008b34972172af8cc5635df3d963dd27183a8f21b7f416d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699588} :answer-field/id #uuid "b218c9c3-cd15-5233-ba41-b80fc27fdad2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699597}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "36301cba-bb7d-56d6-bf60-1510c1ba0e9f" :question/problem "Which diagram represents\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=(y-x)\\,\\mathbf i+(x+y)\\,\\mathbf j\n$$\n\nat $A=(-2,1)$, $B=(1,1)$, and $C=(2,-2)$? All diagrams use one unit per grid interval." :question/worked-solution "Evaluate both components at each point, keeping their order: the $\\mathbf i$ component is horizontal and the $\\mathbf j$ component is vertical.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(-2,1)&=(1-(-2))\\,\\mathbf i+(-2+1)\\,\\mathbf j=3\\,\\mathbf i-\\mathbf j \\\\\n\\mathbf F(1,1)&=(1-1)\\,\\mathbf i+(1+1)\\,\\mathbf j=2\\,\\mathbf j \\\\\n\\mathbf F(2,-2)&=(-2-2)\\,\\mathbf i+(2+(-2))\\,\\mathbf j=-4\\,\\mathbf i.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the arrow at $A$ goes 3 right and 1 down, the arrow at $B$ goes straight up 2 units, and the arrow at $C$ goes straight left 4 units. A zero component removes motion along that axis; it does not remove the other component. Keep each tail at its labeled point and check all three arrows.\n\n![](images/bb/bbb0d965c7ec72ee8008b34972172af8cc5635df3d963dd27183a8f21b7f416d.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699603 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04b6dd27-4b23-5629-928b-935d284ece38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/00/0021413d66ea6423e35f3e2d67083509ce9d5442feed04964586ebe0739727fa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699574} {:answer/id #uuid "1fda1b22-e592-523f-9dfd-32f9952c40d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4b/4bf7b2086637023ea65047fc42646a0bd2f9c4a6ca7f0135470c753038fe721b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699578} {:answer/id #uuid "9cc2f2f7-30dc-55fe-9c20-10e0f5a388ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/90/908a6bdba9f909405af82e26c47e1a61eb8f60968b46a87127dfe8d5e86c34e7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699595} {:answer/id #uuid "ca858bb7-e750-575f-bc89-37871efe3229" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d5/d5b01bd99fe1c60b53fcbda847b5690a45425039558208819a2fe555185b4893.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699598} {:answer/id #uuid "e236aa1c-bc58-5a6d-8304-4edb1207c3a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4c/4cc661c209dd8c9dda698a876e042bb0f5e416e60e42455b62a74d0d0d628933.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca858bb7-e750-575f-bc89-37871efe3229" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d5/d5b01bd99fe1c60b53fcbda847b5690a45425039558208819a2fe555185b4893.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699598} :answer-field/id #uuid "072e2e40-1b7e-58d9-aa18-13c8080cd956" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699575} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb8224bc-dc3a-56ab-946a-b59a25ab983d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb8224bc-dc3a-56ab-946a-b59a25ab983d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699604} :answer-field/id #uuid "37d145c0-20fd-595e-8a23-9c2c7489bea6" :answer-field/key "A x-coordinate" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699581} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c0eb441-049a-5f87-b130-dfbdf32d02c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c0eb441-049a-5f87-b130-dfbdf32d02c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699591} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f02ebf5-96dd-5e0f-990d-9c98edd6cf50" :answer-field/key "A y-coordinate" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699582} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaa43bbe-2893-590f-af62-b85cfc7b45f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaa43bbe-2893-590f-af62-b85cfc7b45f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699596} :answer-field/id #uuid "462fce75-1ca2-543a-a344-f8edc4540e03" :answer-field/key "C x-coordinate" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699583} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd28bbcf-d8bb-5347-a748-62920db04fe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd28bbcf-d8bb-5347-a748-62920db04fe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699605} :answer-field/id #uuid "9050ced3-4b2e-5238-93ad-c870bf2249f8" :answer-field/key "C y-coordinate" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699592} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e5c8a85-65e0-53f7-b1ef-be3e453f084b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e5c8a85-65e0-53f7-b1ef-be3e453f084b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699587} :answer-field/id #uuid "93209eeb-585f-55e6-9089-cb5f9557c4e8" :answer-field/key "B y-coordinate" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699593} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d313c666-4a58-5241-a02c-3619ad7020d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d313c666-4a58-5241-a02c-3619ad7020d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699599} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3ce8e7f-0893-55e4-9093-c35f6e863783" :answer-field/key "B x-coordinate" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699602}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e9f9252b-5e19-5c34-b143-ee99843a434b" :question/problem "Sketch the vector field\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=-xy\\,\\mathbf i+x^2\\,\\mathbf j\n$$\n\nat $A=(-2,1)$, $B=(1,-1)$, and $C=(2,-1)$ by completing both tasks. All diagrams use one unit per grid interval.\n\nEnter the coordinates of the arrowhead for each vector when its tail is at the stated point.\n\nArrowhead from $A$: $(${{A x-coordinate}}$,\\,${{A y-coordinate}}$)$\n\nArrowhead from $B$: $(${{B x-coordinate}}$,\\,${{B y-coordinate}}$)$\n\nArrowhead from $C$: $(${{C x-coordinate}}$,\\,${{C y-coordinate}}$)$\n\nChoose the correct diagram below." :question/worked-solution "First evaluate the field, treating $-xy$ as the negative of the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf F(-2,1)&=-(-2)(1)\\,\\mathbf i+(-2)^2\\,\\mathbf j=2\\,\\mathbf i+4\\,\\mathbf j \\\\\n\\mathbf F(1,-1)&=-(1)(-1)\\,\\mathbf i+1^2\\,\\mathbf j=\\mathbf i+\\mathbf j \\\\\n\\mathbf F(2,-1)&=-(2)(-1)\\,\\mathbf i+2^2\\,\\mathbf j=2\\,\\mathbf i+4\\,\\mathbf j.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors all point up and right, so direction alone cannot select a diagram. Their horizontal and vertical displacements must also match: $(2,4)$ at $A$, $(1,1)$ at $B$, and $(2,4)$ at $C$.\n\nThe field value gives a displacement, not the arrowhead's coordinates. Add each displacement to its tail:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA+\\mathbf F(A)&=(-2+2,\\,1+4)=(0,5),\\\\\nB+\\mathbf F(B)&=(1+1,\\,-1+1)=(2,0),\\\\\nC+\\mathbf F(C)&=(2+2,\\,-1+4)=(4,3).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors at $A$ and $C$ have equal components but different tails and arrowheads. The resulting diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/00/009e26f3566e0a28d8b74b970ed4e18fab0e42079051764e50124cbc43fba278.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a8f93fe-9624-58ca-b181-c8db155547a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4c/4c86c3ffe220532d2e61d7d3eb43328131849ba0551aa197ab5c45e503c3ed5f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699896} {:answer/id #uuid "87d697b9-53b5-570e-a3bd-8089cdbc0605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3d/3dc1cb0a1fc04e960aa082f3519d346f2eb1229106ed76353cb95fbe4f91deb0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699912} {:answer/id #uuid "87de592f-6c0a-5694-aaf9-e6f565b33055" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cb/cb244b77cb36032c0034678bbb3fd2f10d24375b9c87575be92645e34d4dd88a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699913} {:answer/id #uuid "af714f7d-d6f6-5da4-a707-9e28e77ba131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/86/863b21b4ee72557a665bf8d31dac02162934c6bfd1b4e7cccc88787d1dde9d16.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699917} {:answer/id #uuid "e2797b9f-a58c-5f29-8673-6c2b5ebf51c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f9/f9a5c6caec97630e8a14f468b8e51f2cd50cc9880594b5905dd1b92c1b021631.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87d697b9-53b5-570e-a3bd-8089cdbc0605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3d/3dc1cb0a1fc04e960aa082f3519d346f2eb1229106ed76353cb95fbe4f91deb0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699912} :answer-field/id #uuid "71a31d91-bf2d-5121-b1a1-8ff517c99ab0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699909}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "281b2ad3-b25c-5ad0-98e9-0a63349e9d3e" :question/problem "Which diagram represents\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)\\,i+\\left(|x|\\right)\\,j\n$$\n\nat $A=(0,-1)$, $B=(0,1)$, $C=(1,-3)$? All diagrams use one unit per grid interval.\n\nEvaluate both components at each point, then place the tail of its vector at that point." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$. Substitute into each component, then combine the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(0,-1)&=-(-1)\\frac{0}{-1}=0 \\\\\nQ(0,-1)&=-(-1)|0|=0 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(0,-1)&=0 \\\\\nP(0,1)&=-(-1)\\frac{0}{1}=0 \\\\\nQ(0,1)&=-(-1)|0|=0 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(0,1)&=0 \\\\\nP(1,-3)&=-(-1)\\frac{1}{-3}=- \\frac{1}{3} \\\\\nQ(1,-3)&=-(-1)|1|=1 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(1,-3)&=-\\frac{1}{3}\\,i+j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first component gives the horizontal displacement and the second gives the vertical displacement. Place each tail at its labeled point. A zero component gives no displacement along that axis; a zero vector stays at its tail.\n\n![](images/3d/3dc1cb0a1fc04e960aa082f3519d346f2eb1229106ed76353cb95fbe4f91deb0.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699901 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bb29d72-87e6-57ed-932e-7cfd0a03f1e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/59/59bf4b515e94e726d3af8a991cfdfd54927e994e664d87a757534bb430ed92c5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699903} {:answer/id #uuid "5803fb47-99ed-5613-ae31-83bdc384b7f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/aa/aa18b272c87bb5222ba7e66adc7524fc1c517892ba4342fef7a02d565f26c31c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699904} {:answer/id #uuid "6eaeaa7e-f25c-5a2e-918a-3856926dadfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6d/6d9c8a73be1513468cd478684f4e81bd6a058ca847c023245004bdca47704bfd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699908} {:answer/id #uuid "7a8ad149-0e6b-5585-80de-c47a784c2ee2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c1/c1b4d360b19d0239c82bf7c4f03ddcfeb572c896ca9b86e06f2d58576bf6d58f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699910} {:answer/id #uuid "b26fec01-78af-5715-8788-59e6f1ff7c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/be/be050faf24136c77177b5cdeb82fe5a5e0e6dd3245a0604474ea00611c91608d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bb29d72-87e6-57ed-932e-7cfd0a03f1e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/59/59bf4b515e94e726d3af8a991cfdfd54927e994e664d87a757534bb430ed92c5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699903} :answer-field/id #uuid "335ea5a3-58c1-524e-8035-7ad37f471639" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699900}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37ecfed8-4569-5c5e-94c9-a4ff1f97904d" :question/problem "Which diagram represents\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(\\frac{y}{xy+1}\\right)\\,i+\\left(\\frac{x}{xy+1}\\right)\\,j\n$$\n\nat $A=(0,3)$, $B=(1,0)$, $C=(3,-1)$? All diagrams use one unit per grid interval.\n\nEvaluate both components at each point, then place the tail of its vector at that point." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$. Substitute into each component, then combine the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(0,3)&=\\frac{(1)(3)}{(0)(3)+1}=3 \\\\\nQ(0,3)&=\\frac{(1)(0)}{(0)(3)+1}=0 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(0,3)&=3\\,i \\\\\nP(1,0)&=\\frac{(1)(0)}{(1)(0)+1}=0 \\\\\nQ(1,0)&=\\frac{(1)(1)}{(1)(0)+1}=1 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(1,0)&=j \\\\\nP(3,-1)&=\\frac{(1)(-1)}{(3)(-1)+1}=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\nQ(3,-1)&=\\frac{(1)(3)}{(3)(-1)+1}=- \\frac{3}{2} \\\\\n\\mathbf F(3,-1)&=\\frac{1}{2}\\,i-\\frac{3}{2}\\,j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first component gives the horizontal displacement and the second gives the vertical displacement. Place each tail at its labeled point. A zero component gives no displacement along that axis; a zero vector stays at its tail.\n\n![](images/59/59bf4b515e94e726d3af8a991cfdfd54927e994e664d87a757534bb430ed92c5.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699906 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "177a26ed-62f6-5f1a-b955-0f9e1632ef32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dc/dca5659208c862497f2052ddbd5d7672d6336d154c818900cc4fccec425dfec9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699895} {:answer/id #uuid "3a74ddf3-f157-567d-95dc-3894c6539e31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e1/e1d69cfb0de2d24a16d10426d5632cb7d84bddb31628ae84336619cb0cdff9da.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699902} {:answer/id #uuid "b0db5701-fa3c-50e6-b5ec-eb607382a469" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/75/753510ef5f4fed587eb11988029c50b9fb92912045e1bf7b99fd094d1fb14f7a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699918} {:answer/id #uuid "c73b864b-a6e1-5cee-b87d-d73194523892" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/76/76391d7e3fc8332a1dbae465a607eee0ce143f2dd8d272162cf45ab3e374fe19.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699923} {:answer/id #uuid "d82eb334-ce62-5132-a664-dd569aaad933" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8d/8df0c8ea5dc6fe03bf070c2ca8a899715f9b627f11bbb756e8a27cdabdbae663.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d82eb334-ce62-5132-a664-dd569aaad933" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8d/8df0c8ea5dc6fe03bf070c2ca8a899715f9b627f11bbb756e8a27cdabdbae663.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699925} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab3c1670-fbe3-5eb9-bb21-623782d48ebd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699916}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6231ff82-79b5-51d4-ac0f-c977c7f4683e" :question/problem "Which diagram represents\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(y-2x\\right)\\,i+\\left(-2y+4x\\right)\\,j\n$$\n\nat $A=(1,0)$, $B=(0,0)$, $C=(0,-2)$? All diagrams use one unit per grid interval.\n\nEvaluate both components at each point, then place the tail of its vector at that point." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$. Substitute into each component, then combine the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(1,0)&=(0)-(2)(1)=-2 \\\\\nQ(1,0)&=(-2)(0)-(2)(-2)(1)=4 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(1,0)&=-2\\,i+4\\,j \\\\\nP(0,0)&=(0)-(2)(0)=0 \\\\\nQ(0,0)&=(-2)(0)-(2)(-2)(0)=0 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(0,0)&=0 \\\\\nP(0,-2)&=(-2)-(2)(0)=-2 \\\\\nQ(0,-2)&=(-2)(-2)-(2)(-2)(0)=4 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(0,-2)&=-2\\,i+4\\,j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first component gives the horizontal displacement and the second gives the vertical displacement. Place each tail at its labeled point. A zero component gives no displacement along that axis; a zero vector stays at its tail.\n\n![](images/8d/8df0c8ea5dc6fe03bf070c2ca8a899715f9b627f11bbb756e8a27cdabdbae663.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699911 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d1f5735-d5e8-54aa-99bb-1674000106b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fb/fb6f667089062d7c406a208dd2377f9941ce1d39e4206f78f7425f93c7252153.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699897} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9cdd7e-1468-55ab-b80d-d67caf0c41cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/80/80baba867a547b0c71a308ecf0a051d10ec74e494731d00aac1bd42ea25e8a98.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699907} {:answer/id #uuid "b28fb461-6de0-5538-9f14-3cc26f2591fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fa/fa48d5e504372b6cdfbf86cf8a4bd510073cd068ed47a5159ae354c20224c8a0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699920} {:answer/id #uuid "c14d9f4f-2379-502e-9587-7a92270dfae1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ea/ea7815bafb1b211486b44c0cc7de9f64ad69576e925809102e005de3c34d670e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699921} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf6e92c-b5d3-510c-a410-930f6a74bdd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/aa/aa5216de6120e354d0e64a6d03209f70cf611b4417b4e795b11f94e3853b939f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a9cdd7e-1468-55ab-b80d-d67caf0c41cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/80/80baba867a547b0c71a308ecf0a051d10ec74e494731d00aac1bd42ea25e8a98.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699907} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe9fa03a-d43e-5011-b20a-0581b6697399" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699929}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7be3def5-ca38-5d81-817b-90672d97ad53" :question/problem "Which diagram represents\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(3\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi x}{2}\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(-xy\\right)\\,j\n$$\n\nat $A=(0,2)$, $B=(-3,-2)$, $C=(2,-1)$? All diagrams use one unit per grid interval.\n\nEvaluate both components at each point, then place the tail of its vector at that point." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$. Substitute into each component, then combine the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(0,2)&=(3)\\sin(0)=0 \\\\\nQ(0,2)&=(-1)(0)(2)=0 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(0,2)&=0 \\\\\nP(-3,-2)&=(3)\\sin\\left(- \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}\\right)=3 \\\\\nQ(-3,-2)&=(-1)(-3)(-2)=-6 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(-3,-2)&=3\\,i-6\\,j \\\\\nP(2,-1)&=(3)\\sin(\\pi)=0 \\\\\nQ(2,-1)&=(-1)(2)(-1)=2 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(2,-1)&=2\\,j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first component gives the horizontal displacement and the second gives the vertical displacement. Place each tail at its labeled point. A zero component gives no displacement along that axis; a zero vector stays at its tail.\n\n![](images/80/80baba867a547b0c71a308ecf0a051d10ec74e494731d00aac1bd42ea25e8a98.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186699914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ecc6fda-39d2-5890-8c70-ae23d62217fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/47/47d19b0ab827362425b410fbb97374b1ff1e5fb615598893489b2c5cc7f61a65.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699898} {:answer/id #uuid "a1e24318-9c3c-5624-98b3-fb8f796aae5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6a/6ad801d03665b00b88d4ca68d8db3bcd750f534f6cdc91961f452478a241780e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699915} {:answer/id #uuid "c1b18bc2-1c78-548f-b8ea-37598585fef7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/eb/ebfa711c34087c27db58698321ac3fc18bd109752c885afafbf1de8d8131689e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699922} {:answer/id #uuid "d5f0b116-690e-5a42-a252-535567139fce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c0/c0c044853126c7a31383af8110c438d0e185c53ebecdc4086f58322cde8d8d4b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699924} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c3a8dd-0057-5c52-a26e-01328cbbdd91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/21/21b0f5411583f6081934b98d9c01c78c3a17292c2b7b9282e66ed7fe3c2fb3c8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ecc6fda-39d2-5890-8c70-ae23d62217fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/47/47d19b0ab827362425b410fbb97374b1ff1e5fb615598893489b2c5cc7f61a65.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699898} :answer-field/id #uuid "58376643-1a7f-5911-8161-c8d6282d7650" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186699905}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a071c0b2-b12a-59cd-bc7b-1824a457b80f" :question/problem "Which diagram represents\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\left(\\frac{2y}{1-y}\\right)\\,i+\\left(\\frac{x}{y-1}\\right)\\,j\n$$\n\nat $A=(1,-2)$, $B=(-3,0)$, $C=(0,3)$? All diagrams use one unit per grid interval.\n\nEvaluate both components at each point, then place the tail of its vector at that point." :question/worked-solution "Write $\\mathbf F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$. Substitute into each component, then combine the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(1,-2)&=\\frac{(2)(-2)}{1-(-2)}=- \\frac{4}{3} \\\\\nQ(1,-2)&=\\frac{(1)(1)}{(-2)-1}=- \\frac{1}{3} \\\\\n\\mathbf F(1,-2)&=-\\frac{4}{3}\\,i-\\frac{1}{3}\\,j \\\\\nP(-3,0)&=\\frac{(2)(0)}{1-(0)}=0 \\\\\nQ(-3,0)&=\\frac{(1)(-3)}{(0)-1}=3 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(-3,0)&=3\\,j \\\\\nP(0,3)&=\\frac{(2)(3)}{1-(3)}=-3 \\\\\nQ(0,3)&=\\frac{(1)(0)}{(3)-1}=0 \\\\\n\\mathbf F(0,3)&=-3\\,i\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first component gives the horizontal displacement and the second gives the vertical displacement. Place each tail at its labeled point. A zero component gives no displacement along that axis; a zero vector stays at its tail.\n\n![](images/47/47d19b0ab827362425b410fbb97374b1ff1e5fb615598893489b2c5cc7f61a65.png)"}] :knowledge-point/title "Sketching a Two-Dimensional Vector Field"}]}
